# Browser clients

Browser client guides own Wasm packaging, generated TypeScript ABI, the shared browser `Connection`, and client-side WebSocket lifecycle. Axum owns the server routes, upgrade endpoints, protocol implementation, and topic publication.

## Choose a task

| Task | Guide |
|---|---|
| split native and Wasm dependencies, run `wasm-pack`, initialize the package, and call HTTP controllers | <GuideRef slug="clients/browser/setup-and-http">Setup and HTTP</GuideRef> |
| connect JSON-WS or STOMP, invoke generated message clients, and manage subscriptions | <GuideRef slug="clients/browser/websocket-messaging">WebSocket messaging</GuideRef> |

## Shared prerequisites

Keep DTOs and generated client declarations in a library that compiles for `wasm32-unknown-unknown`. Complete setup first: the messaging guide uses the same initialized package and shared `Connection` rather than repeating target dependencies and ABI rules.
